Cell["\<\
z is this difference times -0.5*h0 (since we have not yet multiplied by h0) \
and h0 = hM*dG. The units are a big weird. hM is unit-less because it\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s the measured strain, but h0 is the hypothetical original \
strain, which has units of distance from its scaling factor. In total, \
redshift is unit-less as we\[CloseCurlyQuote]d expect. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.950307782431428*^9, 3.9503078799437447`*^9}, {
